// The positive control (§4/§5): deliberately satisfiable. No constraints
// at all beyond the two typed variables and the goal — any schema where
// `view` can ever be granted at all (a bare `viewer` tuple is enough)
// satisfies this. Its entire purpose is proving the verifier's search can
// actually find a witness when one plainly exists, not just report
// nothing found by default. A verifier that only ever says HOLDS because
// its search is broken is worse than no verifier — this fixture is the
// check against that failure mode. Expected verdict once §5 exists:
// VIOLATED, with a one-tuple witness.
invariant positive_control_view_is_reachable {
  s: user
  o: document

  goal: view(s, o)
}
